Edge: what about `submitId` when stale success? The current draft's submitId (generated at reset) must be kept — do NOT regenerate, otherwise... actually regenerating would also be fine functionally but would mean if the user had already... no, user can't submit while button disabled. But regenerating on stale success is unnecessary and could theoretically cause issues? No real issue, but cleaner to not touch. Actually wait — there IS an issue: if stale success handler regenerates submitId, and the user meanwhile... button is disabled, so no submit in flight for the new draft. Regenerating is harmless. But NOT regenerating is safer and matches "不能...改动新登记" — the submitId is part of the new registration's identity. Don't touch it.

